WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.701
-Kenya Barris, welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.567
Thanks for being here.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.901
I want to talk to you about --

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.434
I want to talk to you
about "You People."

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.000
-Oh, thank you.
-Eddie -- Congratulations.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.434
-Oh, thanks.
-Eddie Murphy, Jonah Hill.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:10.501
It's great.
I want to get into all that.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:11.634
But, first, you were telling me

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.567
about a movie you're doing now
backstage.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.601
You're working on a new film.
-Yes.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.834
-And can we talk about this?
-Yeah, let's talk about it.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.167
-It's a --
It's kind of a reimagining

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.601
of "The Wizard of Oz."

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.667
-Yeah.
-That's a big thing.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.534
-It's a big deal. [ Laughs ]
-It's a big deal.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:27.334
How did you end up there,
and how are you gonna do this?

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.567
-I wanted to --
me and Rashida Jones,

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:32.067
who's my sister --
we wanted to do "The Wiz."

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.267
-Yeah.
-And, you know,

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:34.567
her dad did the music for it,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.501
and we thought
it would be great.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:41.167
And we went to --
the studio who owns the --

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.534
who owns "The Wiz,"
which is --

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.834
probably this studio --
and I love --

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.234
I love the people,
but they were kind of hedging.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.100
And then we realized they were
never going to let us do it,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.834
because they had "Wicked"
coming out,

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.634
and they had invested
so much money in "Wicked."

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.400
-Oh, yeah.
-And so we went to Warner Bros.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.601
And she had to go do some --

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.901
make a ton of money
doing some shows or whatever.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.267
But I really wanted to do it.

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:04.467
And Toby Emmerich,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:05.734
who was running Warner Bros.
at the time,

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.434
that was his favorite movie.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:12.501
And I gave him my pitch of,
like, I think "The Wizard of Oz"

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.834
back in the day was like --
it turned a mirror.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.534
It was like the Dust Bowl,
Great Depression era,

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.534
and it turned a mirror on, like,
society.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.334
That's what it was about.
It was, like, talking about

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.534
self-reliance
and things like that.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.767
I think that this is
the best time

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:27.400
to turn a mirror on society,
because we need to see ourself.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.767
And I was, like, I want to do it
with diverse characters,

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.067
and I really want to sort of,
you know -- she lives --

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.267
the character lives in Inglewood
and something comes up

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:38.234
and she ends up in Underhood,
which is right outside...

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:40.601
[ Light laughter ]
...outside of Oz.

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:41.701
And it takes place from there.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.334
And I'm doing it
with these guys,

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.601
1500 or Nothin' --
like, amazing musicians.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:50.367
And -- But we're writing it
with the music as I'm writing,

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.467
because I feel like
it's the only movie

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:55.033
where each song tells you
what's about to happen.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.100
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.234
-"We're off to see --"
and I saw --

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:58.267
-Yeah,
"We're off to see the Wizard."

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.067
-So literally, like,
hearing, like --

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.901
I didn't realize how melodic
"Somewhere Over the Rainbow"

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.400
was, that you --
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.300
So, like, they're giving me
different motifs.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.534
And like, I've never --
it's all --

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:08.901
-Have you ever written
like that before?

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:12.534
-[ Sighs ] No, but I actually
worked with your guys,

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.334
and we did an amazing
Juneteenth musical.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:18.901
And I realized, like, it was --

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.667
it was something I wanted to do.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:21.801
It was something
I really wanted.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.634
I wanted to, like,
make people think,

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.601
but, also, make 'em feel good

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:28.334
and also make people feel seen
who hadn't been seen, so...

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.767
-Good for you, bud.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.434
-Come on. You keep crushing --
keep hitting homers, man.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:32.701
Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:35.701
Let's talk about
your new comedy,

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:36.934
a new comedy film.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.067
By the way, first of all,
a new comedy film!

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.634
-[ Laughs ] No comedies.
-No one makes comedies anymore.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.834
Let's make a comedy film.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:47.200
Let's go support a comedy.
"You People."

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.033
You're getting great reviews,
buddy.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.868
Here's one from Deadline --
said, "Eddie Murphy,

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.534
Julia Louis-Dreyfus,
Jonah Hill

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:53.734
lead Kenya Barris'

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.834
hysterically funny and smart
feature debut."

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.167
Congratulations, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.167 --> 00:03:00.133
-Thank you so much.
-Dude, rave reviews.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.000
-Rave reviews.
-You co-wrote the script

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.534
with Jonah Hill...
-Yeah.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.033
-...who's very funny,
one of our favorites --

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.200
very funny in this movie.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.968
How did you guys get together?

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:10.400
-So, I've been a fan
of Jonah's forever.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.567
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.968
Like, you know, I grew up
with those Apatow films,

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.400
and you know what I'm saying?
-He's unbelievable.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.734
-"Freaks and Geeks"
and all this stuff.

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:20.234
And we --
I really started getting,

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.968
you know, started talking a lot
when he did "Mid90s."

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.300
'Cause I was like,
"Bro, you killed it."

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.968
-Oh, that was great.
-He killed it.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:27.901
And I was -- So, we, you know,
he was, like, telling me

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.634
he likes the stuff that I do.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.000
He's like --
He likes talking about stuff.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.434
He's like -- He has an idea.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.868
And we -- So it was supposed
to be a 30-minute meeting --

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.801
ended up being three hours
that led to two weeks

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.234
of us putting together a pitch,
and we --

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:42.067
you know, he was dating
this Colombian girl,

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.734
and he talked about, like,

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:46.334
it's not the people
who usually are the problem --

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:49.133
it's the people around them
that are the problem.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:50.868
And then we started talking
about, you know,

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.100
Jewish families
and Black families,

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.801
it's like
the Oppression Olympics.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.567
You know what I'm saying?
Like, who had it --

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.868
-"The Oppression Olympics."
-Who had it worse?

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.200
And we just, literally --

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.033
Like, the point for me --
like, we're both L.A. kids.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.868
I'm from a, you know,

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:03.968
predominantly
Black neighborhood --

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:05.200
he's from a predominantly white,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.934
but the way L.A. geographically
is set up,

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.634
a lot of times, by the time
you get to high school,

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.200
you start mixing the kids --
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.067
And I started finding, like,
you know,

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.701
you have more in common
than you do not.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:18.000
-Yeah.
-And so, we were, like,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.767
let's just, you know,
make this a love letter to L.A.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.167
Like, that really was,
like, you know,

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.267
one of the things
we wanted to do

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:25.267
is make it a love letter
to our culture,

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:27.534
and let's, you know, make it
a love letter to love.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.067
-Yeah.
-And so, I think

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.534
that's what we tried
to set out and do.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.767
And hopefully people, like, it
resonates and people get that.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.033
-It has joke,
joke, joke, joke, joke.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.367
I mean, it is -- Dude,
you came out punching, man.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.667
-Yeah, we swung.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.100
-Every second is a joke,
and it's, like, so good.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.634
And Lauren London?

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.834
-She's the next --
she's Black Julia Roberts.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:48.200
-She's unbelievable in this,
and that is a big discovery.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.100
[ Applause ]
-You know, I feel like it is,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.434
in our community,
in the Black community,

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:53.467
people -- she was --
she was ours.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:54.834
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:57.133
And she had some traumatic
things in her life happen.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.000
And I had to beg her to do this.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.434
-She knocks it out of the park.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:02.667
-She knocked --
And she's just --

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:03.934
I have this thing --

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.400
I think stars are stars
because there's like --

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.267
Julia Roberts, Sandra Bullock,
George Clooney, De Niro

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.434
says the same lines --
you basically --

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:15.467
they're basically the
same person, and you buy them.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:17.400
That's what makes them a star,
something about them.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.601
And I think something about
Lauren --

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:19.901
you just want her to win.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:20.968
-Yeah.
-You want to root for her.

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.434
-I totally agree with you, yeah.

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.567
It's so funny.
How do we set up the movie?

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.667
-It's a love story.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.834
Girl from
Inglewood/Baldwin Hills

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:33.934
whose family is Muslim
has a -- gets --

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.100
has a great meet-cute
with someone from a complete --

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.000
from Brentwood,
a completely different thing.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.667
They come together.

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.234
They really fall for each other.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:44.067
They fall for, like,
what love is really about --

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.801
like, just connection.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.501
And they realize that the hurdle

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.667
is now going to be
their parents.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.701
And that's where the show
kind of takes off.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.234
-Yeah.
I want to show a clip.

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.434
Here's Jonah Hill
and Julia Louis-Dreyfus

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:56.467
in "You People."

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:57.601
Take a look.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.334
-Everyone thinks I'm cool,
I'm hip.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:00.601
-[ Sighs ]

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:02.367
-People think
I'm a very youthful person.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.501
"I get it."

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.434
You know, you're
expressing yourself

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:08.167
with these illustrations,
graffiti all over your body.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.367
Okay, fine.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:12.801
But it is Yom Kippur,
God damn it.

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:14.534
-First of all, can you
please stop saying

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:16.000
"I get it" and using air quotes?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.634
And second of all,
when someone says,

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:18.968
"I'm cool, I get it,"

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.400
they never are cool
and they never get it.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.267
You shouldn't have to say that.
-That's not true in my case.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:26.300
-You won't be able to be buried
in a Jewish cemetery.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.801
-Bubbie, respectfully,
you can take my ashes,

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.167
and you can flush them
down the urinal

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.934
at Dodger Stadium, respectfully.
-What?

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.634
-Oh, so now you're
disrespecting the Dodgers?

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:37.167
-I-I wanna be buried
next to Rihanna.

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:38.501
-Rihanna? What do you --
-Yeah.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:41.601
-Okay, I'm gonna scrape
those tattoos off myself,

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.200
and I'm gonna bury you
in a double-wide coffin with me.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.667
Okay?
How about that?

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.434
-Sounds good.
-Sounds good.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.133
-Yeah, sounds good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:50.634
I mean, have you --

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:54.367
I also should mention Mike Epps.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:57.067
-Mike Epps kills in every scene
in this movie.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:58.901
-Oh, my God.
-That dude was on fire, man.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.868
-Him and Deon Cole...
-Yeah.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:02.167
-...are just like --
it was crazy,

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:04.934
because Eddie is everybody's --
like, you know,

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:06.367
all the comedians,
like, they look up to Eddie.

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:07.467
-Eddie Murphy.

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:09.367
-When Mike came,
he was especially --

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:10.601
he's like,
"I'm 'bout to show off."

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:11.767
You know what I'm saying?

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.467
And literally seeing them
together,

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:15.534
I feel like there's so much
on the cutting-room floor

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.234
that I one day want to put out.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:18.934
It was --
You couldn't stop laughing.

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:21.601
Like, we -- we had to stop --
I had to, like, tell people,

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:23.000
"You've got to leave
if you can't stop laughing."

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.400
-And if you
can get Eddie Murphy to laugh,

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.400
it feels good.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.067
-It feels like scoring
on Jordan.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.634
[ Laughter and applause ]
-It does.

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:29.767
Kenya Barris, everybody.

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:32.167
"You People"
is in select theaters now,

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.400
premieres on Netflix
next Friday.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.400
Go see a comedy
in a movie theater!

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.033
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:39.300
Stick around.
[ Cheers and applause ]

